---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout 
  title="About"
  description="Technical Architect with 11+ years in solution and enterprise architecture, now focused on LLM-powered and agentic systems in production."
>
  <div class="py-16 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">About Me</h1>
        
        <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
            I'm a Technical Architect with 11+ years of experience designing and delivering enterprise and government-scale platforms, from first RFP and solution design through to production. My work sits where architecture meets execution: event-driven microservices, workflow and DAG orchestration, data and streaming pipelines, and the contracts and guardrails that let many teams build safely on one platform.
          </p>
          
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
            Lately, much of that work involves AI. I've architected LLM-driven workflow orchestration, where natural-language intent becomes a validated, human-approved execution plan, and a retrieval-augmented (RAG) assistant grounded in an organisation's own content. I'm designing production-grade agentic AI systems and working through what governance, observability and failure handling they need to be trusted in enterprise environments.
          </p>
          
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
            I write about these trade-offs on the blog. Architecture decisions are easier to get right when they're argued out in the open.
          </p>
          
          <div class="bg-accent-50 dark:bg-accent-900/20 rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-accent-900 dark:text-accent-100">Focus Areas</h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              <li><strong>AI & Agentic Systems:</strong> LLM tool-calling, RAG and agentic workflows designed with schema validation, human-in-the-loop approval and clear failure boundaries.</li>
              <li><strong>Solution & Enterprise Architecture:</strong> Turning business goals and RFPs into target architectures, integration strategy, NFRs and delivery roadmaps that teams can actually build.</li>
              <li><strong>Event-Driven & Distributed Systems:</strong> Microservices, messaging topologies and API/BFF boundaries that stay reliable under load and failure.</li>
              <li><strong>Workflow & Process Orchestration:</strong> Durable, DAG-based orchestration (Temporal) for long-running, multi-step business and machine workflows.</li>
              <li><strong>Data & Streaming Platforms:</strong> ETL/ELT and real-time pipelines (Kafka, Flink, Glue, Snowflake) that feed analytics and AI.</li>
              <li><strong>Platform, Contracts & DevOps:</strong> Contract-first APIs, containerised delivery, CI/CD and hybrid E2E testing that let multiple teams ship safely.</li>
              <li><strong>Technical Leadership:</strong> Architecture reviews, decision records and mentoring that scale design quality beyond one person.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Current Focus</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">
            I lead architecture for complex enterprise and government platforms: robotic workflow orchestration with distributed microservices and Kafka event streaming, digital government platforms with e-services and workflow automation, healthcare data pipelines, social platforms, and B2B e-commerce systems.
          </p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Technology Stack</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
            I work primarily with modern JavaScript/TypeScript ecosystems (Node.js, NestJS, Next.js, React), complemented by experience across multiple languages and platforms for full-stack delivery. For a detailed breakdown, see the <a href="/nitesh-portfolio/skills" class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline">Skills</a> page.
          </p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Education</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2">
            <strong>B.Tech. (Information Technology)</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Engineering College Bikaner / Rajasthan Technical University · 2010–2014
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Let's Connect</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
            Want to compare notes on architecture or AI systems? Get in touch or follow along on the blog.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a
              href="/nitesh-portfolio/contact"
              class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-accent-600 hover:bg-accent-700 text-white font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors"
            >
              Get in Touch
            </a>
            <a
              href="/nitesh-portfolio/blog"
              class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-200 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors"
            >
              Read the Blog
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
